# Author's working notes and original brief. Kept locally, never published:
# personal drafting rather than documentation, and the repo's own docs supersede
# it. IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md is excluded for the same reason plus one more --
# it asserts a completeness that has never been verified by running anything.
intial.md
IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md

# This deployment's persona: the machine the honeypot pretends to be.
# Deliberately not shared. Publishing it would hand anyone the fingerprint --
# banner, hostnames, kernels, shell history -- needed to identify this host.
persona/persona.json

# Agent tooling config. Local to whoever is working on the checkout, and not
# something a public clone should inherit.
.claude/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
admin-dashboard/config/
admin-dashboard/admin-logs/
docker-compose.override.yml

# TLS material -- the Cloudflare origin key must never be committed
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Captured attacker data. Contains third-party credentials; keep it off git.
storage/

# MaxMind GeoLite2 databases: large binaries under their own licence terms.
elastic/geoip/*.mmdb

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.Python
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Redis persistence
dump.rdb
appendonly.aof

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Project website. Deployed from its own host, not from this repo -- and kept
# out of it so the marketing page and the appliance are never entangled.
site/

# Working notes for this checkout. Local only: it names the production path,
# describes what the storage volume holds and explains how the demo relates to
# the appliance -- an accurate description of the deployment, which is exactly
# what should not ship with the code an attacker can already read.
CLAUDE.md

# The public demo. A separate deployment that consumes the built dashboard
# image and shows synthetic data -- see CLAUDE.md. Kept out of the repository
# for the same reason site/ is: it is a different product with a different
# audience, and entangling the two is how real captured credentials end up on
# a public URL.
demo/

# Scratch file for `git commit -F COMMIT_MSG.txt`. PowerShell cannot pipe a
# here-string into `git commit -F-`, so long messages go via a file -- and a
# `git add -A` before the commit will otherwise sweep the message into the
# commit it describes, which is how it landed in 75852a0.
COMMIT_MSG.txt
